<MainLayout title="About | Through My Quiet Lens"><section><div class="wrap page"><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>The person behind the lens.</h1><h2>Why I write</h2><p>I write because writing helps me understand. Through My Quiet Lens is a place to explore what work, leadership, technology, community and everyday life have taught me—often long after the moment itself has passed.</p><h2>My journey</h2><p>I grew up in Chennai and built my career across India, Singapore and the United States. My professional path has centred on commercial leadership and mission-critical infrastructure, but many of the ideas here come from quieter places: classrooms, negotiations, community projects and conversations around a table.</p><h2>Family</h2><p>My wife and daughter shape how I see ambition, learning and what matters beyond work. They may appear in these pages when their perspectives are part of the story, while their privacy remains theirs.</p><h2>Percy & Pluto</h2><p>I spent more than forty years without a dog. Then Percy and Pluto arrived and quietly changed how I think about patience, presence, routine, trust and joy. They occasionally appear in my writing—not because this is a site about dogs, but because some of life's best teachers have four legs.</p><h2>Professional background</h2><p>I have spent more than fifteen years building markets, customer relationships and commercial growth across Asia-Pacific and the United States. For the detailed professional version, find me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/gpraveen1882/">LinkedIn</a>.</p></div></section></MainLayout><style>.page{max-width:760px}.page h1{font-size:clamp(3rem,7vw,5rem);line-height:1.05}.page h2{font-size:2rem;margin-top:3rem}.page p{font-size:1.08rem}</style>
